conventions:
Plain modern JavaScript as ES modules (`.mjs`), focused on the LANGUAGE (not Node runtime APIs). The code under test is `solution.mjs` with named exports, in starter/, solution/ and every bugs/<name>/. Tests are `tests/*.test.mjs` using `node:test` and `node:assert/strict`, and load the target with:

    const { fn } = await import(`../${process.env.TARGET ?? "starter"}/solution.mjs`);

Name tests descriptively: the name is what `bugs[].expect` matches. Pass a teaching message as the last assert argument. A starter stub throws `new Error("TODO")`. Favor idiomatic JS: immutability, Map/Set, iterators, destructuring, closures, async/await, precise equality.
